{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And see.</b> For the making of the menorah requires wisdom and seeing with the vision of the heart, how all the vessels shall be made from a single ingot:" "The word מָרְאָה is foreign and not according to the usual pattern — cast (II Samuel 20:21) — for there is no active participle for the root ראה, but rather נראה alone, and this is so because the one who sees does not act but only receives an image, and one versed in natural science will understand this. And before I speak of the Tabernacle — which also had kerubim curtains — I shall give you a principle upon which to rely:" "<b>Said Abraham the author:</b> Every existent is in two ways: one, that it is a body having length, breadth, and depth, and it has six faces — from length come front and back, from breadth right and left, and from height above and below. And there is an existent that is not a body, and these are the holy angels of HaShem, also the soul of man. And these two ways HaShem alone created, and there is no power in a created being to create a substance that is a body, let alone an existent that is not a body and is more honored. Also, there is no power to annihilate it until it ceases and is no longer existent. And there is a thing dependent upon an existent and leaning upon it, not found on its own — and that is form. It too is in two ways: one, standing and not departing, like the form of the holy ones, and wisdom in the soul, and also in bodies, like the heat of fire and the fluidity of water. And the other way, accidental — they do not stand but are transformed, exchanged, depart, and cease. And such things can man make. Therefore the honored HaShem — it is impossible that He have a likeness or form, neither standing nor passing. For HaShem created the substance of every thing, for every form is either standing or accidental. And I shall give you one analogy: the eclipses of the moon, when the shadow of the earth enters between it and the sun at the head of the ecliptic or at its tail. And I shall give you another analogy: we know that the power of the soul is in the entire body, and there are places in the body of man where there are nerves issuing from the brain that sense more than others, such as the eyes and the ears, whereas the bones and also the liver do not sense. Now the heart received the power of the soul more than all the organs of the body; therefore many organs serve it. And so the honored HaShem — we know that His glory fills the whole world, only there are places where the power of HaShem is seen in them more than in other places. And this is on account of two things: one, according to the disposition of the nature of the recipient, and the second, according to a supernal power that is above the head of the recipient. Therefore a place was chosen for the Temple. And if HaShem has given you wisdom in your heart, you will understand the secret of the Ark and the cover and the kerubim that spread wings, and outside the veil — the matter of the menorah and the incense altar and the table, and outside the entrance of the Tabernacle — the altar of burnt offering and all its vessels, and the basin and its base. And these things are the glory of Elohim, and on account of this I have hinted to you, for there are in our generation people wise in their own eyes who may mock my words. And one who knows the secret of his soul and the nature of his body will be able to know the matters of the supernal world, for man is a likeness of a small world, and he was the end of creation on earth. And a sign for the matter: with the greatest He began, and with the smallest He concluded. And the Gaon [Saadia] mentioned that eighteen things are in the Tabernacle, which is an intermediate world, and likewise in the supernal world, and so the small world. Behold, the principle: every kerub was made to receive the supernal power, also so that the discerning may learn, and there is no need to elaborate:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:40.065855398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}